{"base_rate":0.291866028708134,"brier":0.19597033492822968,"bss":0.051818763845812854,"bss_hi":0.17745177001651977,"bss_lo":-0.11053938833528977,"country":"CA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1754066985645933,"ess":436.7542725173208,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Edmonton</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Edmonton rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>71%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 627 days, 2024-04-27 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nEDMONTON 5.4 SSW, 7.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.05, ranked 104 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(94&ndash;107) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>184</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>13%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>126</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Edmonton</b> <span class=\"muted\">CA</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.05</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>94&ndash;107\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>627 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Edmonton &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Edmonton\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.500652173913046,376.0652173913044 87.9579104477612,322.23880597014926 138.50645161290322,258.7096774193549 199.2518032786885,191.04918032786884 276.484375,114.6875 371.82380952380953,35.33333333333337 410.9885714285714,18.0 410.9885714285714,23.77777777777777 371.82380952380953,87.33333333333331 276.484375,200.0 199.2518032786885,280.55737704918033 138.50645161290322,335.0322580645161 87.9579104477612,371.13432835820896 59.500652173913046,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"275.7607655502392\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"275.7607655502392\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.500652173913046,360.2391304347826 87.9579104477612,333.1044776119403 138.50645161290322,323.2903225806452 199.2518032786885,304.42622950819674 276.484375,245.5 371.82380952380953,231.7777777777778 410.9885714285714,122.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 184 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.500652173913046\" cy=\"360.2391304347826\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 13% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"87.9579104477612\" cy=\"333.1044776119403\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 23%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"138.50645161290322\" cy=\"323.2903225806452\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 40%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"199.2518032786885\" cy=\"304.42622950819674\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"276.484375\" cy=\"245.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 89%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"371.82380952380953\" cy=\"231.7777777777778\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 126 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.9885714285714\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(29%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Edmonton the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.18) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.10).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>133</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>-0.097</td><td class='num'>22.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>167</td><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'>0.010</td><td class='num'>14.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>168</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.033</td><td class='num'>15.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>159</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.181</td><td class='num'>14.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":53.55014,"lon":-113.46871,"n":627,"n_cities":109,"name":"Edmonton","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00